  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `EditOperationParams` applies a new law, `OpParams::with_start_side_entry` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/start_side_entry.rs`).\n- The law acts on a 2D Offset only. It acts when one edit moves \"Pass starts at\" from Auto to Inside or Outside, and the entry is Helix before and after the edit. Then the same edit sets Arc.\n- The GUI page, MCP `edit_operation`, and the cutting-data and stock edits use the same constructor. Thus each door gets the law.\n- One undo restores Auto and Helix together.\n- The user's own choice stays:\n  - an entry that the same edit changes;\n  - a Plunge or Ramp set before the start side moves;\n  - a Helix kept on Inside that moves to Outside;\n  - a Helix that the user selects again on an Inside or Outside pass;\n  - the entry when the start side goes back to Auto.\n- The seed (Auto, Helix) does not change. `docs/decisions/3843-start-side-arc.md` records why.\n\n## Cause\n\n`seed_offset2d` seeds Helix for every new 2D Offset. A change of the start side did not change the entry. After #3748, a start-side pass with Helix gives the `EntryNotRecommended` warning. The maintainer said on #3741: \"an outside cut would default to a ARC or straight approach in the plane of its cut\".\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests:\n- `offset_pass_start::start_side_entry::a_start_side_edit_of_a_seeded_offset_takes_arc_and_undo_restores_helix` (command and undo, Inside and Outside).\n- `offset_pass_start::start_side_entry::mcp_start_side_edit_takes_arc_and_a_later_helix_choice_stays` (MCP door).\n- lib `operation::types::start_side_entry::tests::a_seeded_offset_moved_to_a_start_side_takes_arc`.\n- lib `operation::types::start_side_entry::tests::a_user_choice_of_entry_stays`.\n\nRed before the fix: the two integration pins failed on the code without the call in `edit.rs`. The failure text: `assertion left == right failed: Inside enters in the plane of its cut; left: (Inside, Helix); right: (Inside, Arc)`. The MCP pin failed at the `\"entry\":\"arc\"` assertion.\n\nMutations (each red, then restored and green):\n- Remove the `before == Helix` guard: `a_user_choice_of_entry_stays` fails.\n- Remove the \"from Auto\" guard: `a_user_choice_of_entry_stays` fails.\n\nCommands on the final head `215d44a52`, base upstream/main `415440375`:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 34 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only \"app suites: example_catalog\"`: ok. `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`: ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate test pass_start --crate camcraft-ui`: ui lib ok.\n- The ignored `offset_pass_start` heavy tests (release step): ok.\n\nHeavy lanes: not run in full. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 64 app steps. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a P3 PR no heavy step, so the light lane ran in its place.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suites ran and pass. No `*.nc`, `*.cl` or `examples/catalog/**` file changed. The law acts only in an edit, and no golden makes a 2D Offset through a start-side edit.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI Lead in page by hand. The page calls the same `EditOperationParams`, and the ui `pass_start` tests pass. No screenshot: the page layout does not change.\n- The `EntryNotRecommended` warning itself. It comes from #3748, which is not on main yet. When #3748 merges, the seed Helix on a start side no longer reaches the warning through an edit.\n- Pocket and 2D Adaptive. The issue names 2D Offset only.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `crates/app/src/commands/operation/edit.rs` or `crates/app/src/operation/types/`. #3748 (claimed, no PR yet) changes the warning and the Lead in page, not the edit command.\n\nNew test file: `crates/app/tests/offset_pass_start/start_side_entry.rs` is a submodule of the existing `offset_pass_start` suite. It adds no test binary.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: 2D Offset: a change of \"Pass starts at\" from Auto to Inside or Outside now sets the Arc lead-in when the lead-in is still the default Helix.\n\nFixes #3843\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
